IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgb2-s161-issue-of-shares`

-- Tests for s 161. Every expected value is written from the text of the section, beside the assertion, before it was run.

§ `s 161(1) the bar and the regulative rule`

-- No prior approval: the directors "must not ... exercise any power of the company to issue shares": barred.
#ASSERT `s 161(1) the section bars the directors from exercising the power of the company to issue shares` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- With prior approval the section bars nothing; it grants nothing either: NOTHING (not JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `s 161(1) the section bars the directors from exercising the power of the company to issue shares` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- EXPECT BREACH. BREACH path: the directors exercise the power with no approval.
#TRACE `s 161(1) the directors must not exercise the power of the company to issue shares without the company's prior approval` "Alice Tan" FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "Alice Tan" DOES `s 161(1) exercise a power of the company to issue shares` AT 1

-- EXPECT FULFILLED. With the approval in hand the rule has nothing left to forbid.
#TRACE `s 161(1) the directors must not exercise the power of the company to issue shares without the company's prior approval` "Alice Tan" TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "Alice Tan" DOES `s 161(1) exercise a power of the company to issue shares` AT 1

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL. No approval and no issue: the prohibition is still standing.
#TRACE `s 161(1) the directors must not exercise the power of the company to issue shares without the company's prior approval` "Alice Tan" FALSE AT 0 WITH

§ `s 161(2) the forms an approval may take`

#ASSERT `s 161(2) the approval is of a form the subsection allows` `s 161(2) confined to a particular exercise of the power` `s 161(2) unconditional` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(2) the approval is of a form the subsection allows` `s 161(2) applying to the exercise of the power generally` `s 161(2) subject to conditions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Outside the two named scopes the text does not say (list not closed): NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 161(2) the approval is of a form the subsection allows` `s 161(2) some other scope` `s 161(2) unconditional` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 161(2) the approval is of a form the subsection allows` `s 161(2) applying to the exercise of the power generally` `s 161(2) some other kind of condition` EQUALS NOTHING

-- A general, unconditional approval covers any exercise.
#ASSERT `s 161(2) the exercise of the power falls within the approval` `s 161(2) applying to the exercise of the power generally` FALSE `s 161(2) unconditional` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A confined approval covers its own exercise, and (the text being silent) the answer for another exercise is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 161(2) the exercise of the power falls within the approval` `s 161(2) confined to a particular exercise of the power` TRUE `s 161(2) unconditional` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(2) the exercise of the power falls within the approval` `s 161(2) confined to a particular exercise of the power` FALSE `s 161(2) unconditional` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A conditional approval covers the exercise only when its conditions are met.
#ASSERT `s 161(2) the exercise of the power falls within the approval` `s 161(2) applying to the exercise of the power generally` FALSE `s 161(2) subject to conditions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(2) the exercise of the power falls within the approval` `s 161(2) applying to the exercise of the power generally` FALSE `s 161(2) subject to conditions` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 161(3) how long an approval continues in force`

-- Approval given 10 March 2026; the next AGM concludes on 30 April 2026; the AGM must be held by 30 June 2026: the earlier, 30 April 2026.
#ASSERT `s 161(3) the last day on which the approval continues in force` (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS Date 30 4 2026
-- Whichever is the earlier: here the period for holding the meeting ends first.
#ASSERT `s 161(3) the last day on which the approval continues in force` (Date 30 9 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS Date 30 6 2026
-- If both fall on one day, that day.
#ASSERT `s 161(3) the last day on which the approval continues in force` (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS Date 30 6 2026

-- In force on the day it was given and every day up to the last day (the day of the concluding meeting counted: fork F-161-3).
#ASSERT `s 161(3) the approval is in force on the day` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(3) the approval is in force on the day` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The day after the last day, the approval has ended: the text fixes the period in its own words: JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 161(3) the approval is in force on the day` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A day before the approval was given: the text is silent.
#ASSERT `s 161(3) the approval is in force on the day` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Revoked in general meeting before the day: no longer in force, even inside the period.
#ASSERT `s 161(3) the approval is in force on the day` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 161(4) shares issued after the approval has ceased`

#ASSERT `s 161(4) the directors may issue the shares although the approval has ceased to be in force` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Each element missing in turn: NOTHING (a grant whose "if" gate failed).
#ASSERT `s 161(4) the directors may issue the shares although the approval has ceased to be in force` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 161(4) the directors may issue the shares although the approval has ceased to be in force` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 161(4) the directors may issue the shares although the approval has ceased to be in force` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 161(5) section 186`

#ASSERT `s 161(5) section 186 applies to the resolution` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(5) section 186 applies to the resolution` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 161(6) an issue in contravention is void`

-- No approval at all, and no s 161(4) offer: the issue contravenes the section.
#ASSERT `s 161 the issue of shares was made in contravention of the section` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Approval given, in force and covering the exercise: no contravention (the section says no more: NOTHING).
#ASSERT `s 161 the issue of shares was made in contravention of the section` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Approval given but it had lapsed, and the shares were not issued under s 161(4): contravention.
#ASSERT `s 161 the issue of shares was made in contravention of the section` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Approval given but the exercise lies outside it: contravention.
#ASSERT `s 161 the issue of shares was made in contravention of the section` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Approval lapsed but the s 161(4) route applies: not a contravention.
#ASSERT `s 161 the issue of shares was made in contravention of the section` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 161(6) the issue of shares is void` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(6) the issue of shares is void` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 161(6) the consideration given for the shares is recoverable` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(6) the consideration given for the shares is recoverable` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 161(7) liability to compensate, and the 2 years`

#ASSERT `s 161(7) the director is liable to compensate the company and the person to whom the shares were issued` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(7) the director is liable to compensate the company and the person to whom the shares were issued` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(7) the director is liable to compensate the company and the person to whom the shares were issued` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(7) the director is liable to compensate the company and the person to whom the shares were issued` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Issue on 15 January 2025: the 2 years run to 15 January 2027 (period P1: the day of the issue is not counted).
#ASSERT `s 161(7) the 2 years bar the proceedings to recover the loss, damages or costs` (Date 15 1 2025) (Date 15 1 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 161(7) the 2 years bar the proceedings to recover the loss, damages or costs` (Date 15 1 2025) (Date 16 1 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 161(7) the 2 years bar the proceedings to recover the loss, damages or costs` (Date 15 1 2025) (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Leap day: issue on 29 February 2024; two years later add years clamps to 28 February 2026 (P4): 28 February 2026 is in time, 1 March 2026 is not.
#ASSERT `s 161(7) the 2 years bar the proceedings to recover the loss, damages or costs` (Date 29 2 2024) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 161(7) the 2 years bar the proceedings to recover the loss, damages or costs` (Date 29 2 2024) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
